        ['q'=>'Does finasteride really work for hair loss?','a'=>'Clinical trials show that finasteride 1mg stops hair loss in approximately 83% of men and promotes regrowth in around 66% after two years. It works by reducing DHT, the hormone responsible for follicle miniaturisation.'],
        ['q'=>'How long before I see results with finasteride?','a'=>'It typically takes 3–6 months before any visible improvement. Full results are usually seen at 12 months. It must be taken daily — stopping the medication will result in hair loss resuming within 6–12 months.'],
        ['q'=>'Can women take finasteride?','a'=>'Finasteride is not currently licensed for female use in the UK, though some clinicians prescribe it off-label for women with androgenetic alopecia. It is contraindicated in women of childbearing potential due to risks to a male foetus.'],
        ['q'=>'What is minoxidil and does it work?','a'=>'Minoxidil is a topical treatment available without prescription that stimulates hair follicles and prolongs the growth phase. It is effective for both male and female pattern hair loss when used consistently.'],
        ['q'=>'Can I take finasteride and use minoxidil at the same time?','a'=>'Yes — combining finasteride and minoxidil is a common approach and some evidence suggests they work synergistically. Our prescribers can advise on the combination that is right for you.'],
